# Error Handling

## Structured Logging

```typescript
import { logger } from "~/shared/lib/logger";

// ✅ Use logger (not console)
logger.info("Operation successful", { userId: user.id });
logger.error("Operation failed", {
  message: error.message,
  stack: error.stack,
});

// ❌ NEVER use console
console.log("Debug"); // FORBIDDEN in production
```

## Error Tracking

```typescript
import { defaultErrorTracker } from "~/shared/lib";

try {
  await riskyOperation();
} catch (error) {
  const err = error as Error;

  // ✅ Log structured
  logger.error("Operation failed", {
    message: err.message,
    stack: err.stack,
  });

  // ✅ Track with service
  defaultErrorTracker.captureException(err, {
    tags: { source: "server", operation: "risky" },
  });

  // ✅ Re-throw or handle
  throw new TRPCError({
    code: "INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR",
    cause: err
  });
}
```

## tRPC Errors

```typescript
import { TRPCError } from "@trpc/server";

// ✅ Use tRPC error codes
throw new TRPCError({ code: "UNAUTHORIZED" });
throw new TRPCError({ code: "BAD_REQUEST", cause: zodError });
throw new TRPCError({ code: "FORBIDDEN" });
throw new TRPCError({ code: "NOT_FOUND" });
```

## Server-Side Error Handling

```typescript
export default async function Page() {
  try {
    await api.posts.getLatest.prefetch();
  } catch (error) {
    // ✅ Log but don't throw - graceful degradation
    logger.error("Prefetch failed", { error });
    // Let client component handle fetching
  }

  return <Component />;
}
```
